WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.201
[music playing]

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.904
NARRATOR: Seti the first was the
father of our friend Ramesses

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.373
the Great.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:10.243
Just like his son, he was a
hugely successful pharaoh.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.146
But in father-son rivalry,
there's one category where

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:17.217
he wins hands down, his mummy.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.486
Because Seti the
first boasts some

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.088
of the finest
mummification work in all

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.591
of ancient Egyptian history.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.993
Mummification is an
incredible process

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.362
of drying out and
embalming the body

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.899
to preserve it, ready for
its journey to immortality

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.235
in the afterlife.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:39.973
Key to it all was the
preparation of the body.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.810
Typically, your brain is pulled
out through your nostrils

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.579
with an iron hook.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.515
Next, all of your
major organs are

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.817
removed apart from the heart.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.586
Ancient Egyptians believed this
was the center of your being.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.492
These organs are then
preserved in special jars,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.662
so they can be reunited with
their owner in the afterlife.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.464
[music playing]

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.203
Your body is then covered in
a salt called natron and left

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.272
to dry for up to 40 days.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.174
[music playing]

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.377
Finally, the now mummified
body is wrapped head

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.947
to foot in hundreds of meters
of linen bandages attached

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:25.251
with a glue, and magical spells
are cast to protect the mummy

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:30.056
and prepare it for safe
arrival in the afterlife.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:33.359
But Seti's mummy is unusual.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.729
His face is incredibly
well-preserved.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.566
He looks almost
perfect, not what you

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:44.904
might expect from a body
over 3,000 years old.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:49.709
But frankly, Seti's has had
quite a lot of work done.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.079
Unlocking the secrets behind
Seti's youthful good looks

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.749
is professor of
radiology Sahar Saleem.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:02:01.254
I always looked at his mummy
and I said, "This is no mummy.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:05.358
This is a sleeping
beauty," and I've always

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:08.661
wondered, what was his secrets?

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:17.470
The secrets revealed to me that
the ancient Egyptians were very

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.974
efficient as plastic surgeons.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.842
So was it really
plastic surgery?

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.143
Yeah.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.547
And they actually placed
feathers around the nose

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.683
and the mouth, in this
region, in the cheeks,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.085
and even in the temporal.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:35.455
What does this tell you about
their ideas of ancient beauty

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.323
for men as well as for women?

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:42.262
The ancient Egyptian would
like to look like his gods.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.665
There is something very,
very charismatic about him.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:51.271
He was the most well-mummified
person from ancient Egypt

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.306
that I've ever looked at.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.542
I love the way
you talk about him.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.210
I bet you wish you'd met him.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.144
Definitely.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.245
We will meet one day.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.180
Yeah, in the afterlife.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.515
Brilliant.
Brilliant.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.349
Well, good luck.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.418
[laughs]

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.353
NARRATOR: Egyptians
beautified Seti's mummy

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.822
to make sure it was in
the best possible shape

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.991
to travel to the afterlife.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:16.380
Once there, Seti would need a
stunning home for all eternity.

